    "title": "Ex-Falcons RB Cordarrelle Patterson Arrested for Domestic Violence - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By paige.boyd ,\n11 hours ago\nSource: Getty Images / Sevier County Jail Cordarrelle Patterson , an NFL running back who played for the Atlanta Falcons , was arrested Saturday (Oct. 17) in Tennessee for domestic violence.\nAs reported by TMZ , Patterson was booked after police in Sevier County received a call about a domestic disturbance. According to the arrest warrant, Patterson’s wife, Taylor Quick, told officers that Patterson assaulted her.\nAllegedly, Patterson grabbed his wife’s hair and left upper arm. An officer noticed bruising on Quick’s arm upon initial contact. “The victim expressed fear for her safety of herself and children as a result of the defendant’s actions,” the report said.\nPatterson was booked in Sevier County Jail, where he smiled for his mugshot photo. He was ultimately released on $1000 bond.\nPatterson is a four-time Pro Bowl running back and kick specialist who played for the Falcons from 2021 to 2023. He played for six seasons during his career and won a Super Bowl with the New England Patriots in 2019.\nLast year, he was released by the Pittsburgh Steelers after being limited to 13 games in 2024 due to an ankle injury.",
    "summary": "Source: Getty Images / Sevier County Jail Cordarrelle Patterson , an NFL running back who played for the Atlanta Falcons , was arrested Saturday (Oct. 17) in Tennessee for domestic violence. As reported by TMZ , Patterson was booked after police in Sevier County received a call about a domestic disturbance. “The victim expressed fear for her safety of herself and children as a result of the defendant’s actions,” the report said. Patterson is a four-time Pro Bowl running back and kick specialist who played for the Falcons from 2021 to 2023.",
